n a Google-integrated ecosystem.Key ResponsibilitiesData Analysis \u0026amp; Dashboards: Process complex datasets using SQL, Python, and Google Sheets, and build interactive reports using Tableau, Power BI, or Looker Studio.AI-First Automation \u0026amp; MCP Integration: Design and deploy Model Context Protocol (MCP) standards and LLM integrations to allow AI agents to safely connect with enterprise data sources and execute multi-step workflows.Advanced Scripting: Build robust data pipelines and complex automations using Python, and streamline day-to-day operations using JavaScript and Google Apps Script across Google Workspace.ETL \u0026amp; Data Governance: Manage basic ETL frameworks, data validation, reconciliation, and consistency across platforms.Stakeholder Collaboration: Translate complex technical findings into clear insights using Google Slides or PowerPoint for cross-functional teams.Candidate RequirementsCore Technical SkillsExperience: 5 to 8+ years of professional experience in a data analysis, business intelligence, or data-driven role.Programming \u0026amp; Databases: Solid foundation in Python and SQL / Google SQL for data extraction, manipulation, and pipeline creation.Google Ecosystem \u0026amp; AI Tooling: Hands-on experience with Google Sheets, Looker Studio, Gemini models, and LLM APIs, alongside workflow automation via JavaScript / Google Apps Script.Modern Frameworks: Familiarity with Model Context Protocol (MCP) standards for dynamic context sharing and tool orchestration.BI \u0026amp; Visualization: Expertise in data visualization platforms like Tableau, Power BI, or Looker Studio.Soft Skills \u0026amp; MindsetAnalytical Thinking: Naturally curious with high attention to detail and a passion for independent problem-solving.Communication: Excellent verbal and written communication skills to convey findings effectively to technical and non-technical stakeholders.","Senior Data Analyst - AI \u0026 Automation",null,null,0,[["organization","Qual